{"title":"Dihedral group","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The dihedral groups <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875585a6a63aefa42d6781cc6f9220b517cf85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> are an infinite family of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Group\" title=\"Group\">groups</a> which are in general <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Noncommutative\" title=\"Noncommutative\">noncommutative</a>. Each dihedral group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875585a6a63aefa42d6781cc6f9220b517cf85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is defined to be the group of linear symmetries of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polygon\" title=\"Regular polygon\">regular</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dihedral_group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_(group_theory)\" title=\"Order (group theory)\">order</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875585a6a63aefa42d6781cc6f9220b517cf85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.</li>\n<li>The group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875585a6a63aefa42d6781cc6f9220b517cf85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Presentation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Presentation (page does not exist)\">presentation</a> in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c4297085e5e9a71343140c076a31c3966bb936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle r, s\\mid r^n = 1, s^2 = 1, srs = r^{-1}\\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"21\" />.</li>\n<li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd69ad8f022ee1b5894dee7cafb68305b47c9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/9875585a6a63aefa42d6781cc6f9220b517cf85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is noncommutative.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dihedral_group&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetric_group\" title=\"Symmetric group\">Symmetric group</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_group\" title=\"Cyclic group\">Cyclic group</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rotation\" title=\"Rotation\">Rotation</a><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Dihedral_group&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017091510\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 62/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1597/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.350      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.350      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19575:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017091510 and revision id 216867. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}